# ==============================================================================
# Sweet Cravings Homemade Desserts — Environment Configuration
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. DATABASE CONFIGURATION (Dual-Mode)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# For Local Development / Self-Hosted VPS:
# Leave both empty. The app automatically uses built-in SQLite (data/sweetcravings.db)
# with zero setup, zero network overhead, and zero cost.

# For 100% FREE Serverless Hosting on Vercel / Netlify / Cloudflare:
# Create a free Turso account at https://turso.tech (9GB free, 1 billion reads/month)
# Run:
#   turso db create sweetcravings
#   turso db show sweetcravings --url
#   turso db tokens create sweetcravings
# Paste them here:
TURSO_DATABASE_URL=
TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. OPERATOR ADMIN SECURITY
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Password for the sister / kitchen operator to access /admin.
# - Set a long random password here (or in your hosting provider's env vars).
# - NEVER commit a real password to git, and never share it in chat or docs.
# - If this is empty or missing, admin login is disabled (fails closed).
# - Generate one with: openssl rand -base64 24
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. INSTANT TELEGRAM KITCHEN ALERTS (100% Free)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Create a free bot via @BotFather on Telegram, paste credentials here or enter
# them through the Admin Settings dashboard (/admin/settings)
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. APP BASE URL
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
